// Reactive `for`s along a tree follow their events where the tree has
// links: from a node with an event up to its parent (a trigger on a
// child's, from the leaves), down to its children, and on to the sibling
// after it (a trigger on the sibling before's), each passing on what its
// body changed (or added into its parent); the nodes without a parent
// are come to by their rows, and a node that has other children or
// siblings than before is come to itself. A trigger on the node two
// arrows up is followed two levels down, also from a node that is put
// under another. And the same with every `for` depth first, where the
// events are followed in the order that is worked out for that.
// Inputs/tree_follow.ent works a wide tree out that way and, without
// triggers, by going through all of it, in every frame of forty in which
// sizes change, the order of siblings, a leaf goes and a node moves with
// all under it: the two never disagree. (Leaving out any one of the
// marks that following sets makes them disagree.)
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/tree_follow.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.out
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/tree_follow.ent 2>/dev/null | cmp - %t.out
// RUN: FileCheck %s --input-file=%t.out
// RUN: sed 's/bottom up In/bottom up dfs In/; s/top down In/top down dfs In/' \
// RUN:     %S/Inputs/tree_follow.ent > %t.dfs.ent
// RUN: grep -c "dfs In" %t.dfs.ent | grep -q 9
// RUN: %ent run %t.dfs.ent 2>/dev/null | cmp - %t.out
// RUN: ent-translate --import-ent %t.dfs.ent -I %S/../../devices -o %t.dfs.mlir
// RUN: ent-opt %t.dfs.mlir "--ent-lower-to-loops=explain=1" -o /dev/null 2>&1 \
// RUN:   | grep -c "remark: follows its events" | grep -q 4
// The same over a tree whose rows are kept in its order, in one archetype
// and (the leaves given a component more) in two: followed there too, in
// an order worked out from the tree's edges.
// RUN: sed 's/ tree ordered by / tree sorted ordered by /' \
// RUN:     %S/Inputs/tree_follow.ent > %t.sorted.ent
// RUN: grep -q "tree sorted ordered" %t.sorted.ent
// RUN: %ent run %t.sorted.ent 2>/dev/null | cmp - %t.out
// RUN: sed 's/else { 2 } },$/else { 2 } }, Leaf { n: 0 },/' %t.sorted.ent > %t.two.ent
// RUN: grep -q "Leaf { n: 0 }," %t.two.ent
// RUN: %ent run %t.two.ent 2>/dev/null | cmp - %t.out
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %t.two.ent 2>/dev/null | cmp - %t.out
// RUN: ent-translate --import-ent %t.two.ent -I %S/../../devices -o %t.two.mlir
// RUN: ent-opt %t.two.mlir "--ent-lower-to-loops=explain=1" -o /dev/null 2>&1 \
// RUN:   | grep -c "remark: follows its events" | grep -q 4
// RUN: ent-translate --import-ent %S/Inputs/tree_follow.ent \
// RUN:     -I %S/../../devices -o %t.mlir
// RUN: ent-opt %t.mlir "--ent-lower-to-loops=explain=1" -o /dev/null 2>&1 \
// RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=EXPLAIN

// The `for` from the leaves, the one from the roots, the one that adds
// into its parent and the one that reacts to the node two above it; not
// the one whose way up is the nearest node that has two components.
// EXPLAIN:      remark: follows its events along the tree
// EXPLAIN-NEXT: leaves first on [changed @Node "base", changed @Lazy "w" down @In
// EXPLAIN:      remark: follows its events along the tree
// EXPLAIN-NEXT: changed @Lazy "x" before @In
// EXPLAIN:      remark: follows its events along the tree
// EXPLAIN-NEXT: !ent.ref<@LazyTop, mut, parent @In>) cascade @In leaves first
// EXPLAIN:      remark: follows its events along the tree
// EXPLAIN-NEXT: changed @Node "base" up @In hops 2]
// EXPLAIN:      remark: goes through its whole tree on each run
// EXPLAIN-NEXT: changed @Node "base" up @In path {{\[\[}}"parent", @In], ["up", @In, @Node, @Slot]]]

// CHECK-NOT:  wrong {{[1-9]}}
// CHECK:      1: wrong 0 runs 979
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: wrong 0 runs 450
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: wrong 0 runs 66
// Nothing changed: nothing ran.
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: wrong 0 runs 0
// CHECK:      40: wrong 0 runs 228
